    "narrative": "Our primary offensive catalyst today is **Tyler Soderstrom**, who paces the squad with a 72.72 efficiency score. The combination of a favorable 4.39 xERA matchup against McGreevy and a 10% park factor bump makes him our must-start anchor. Alongside him, **Brice Turang** earns a strong 64.63 rating; his placement in the #2 hole provides a critical buffer for our team\u2019s stolen base aggression, and he remains the most reliable engine in the lineup against Canning. While **Josh Naylor** faces a respectable 3.90 xERA arm, his 61.45 score is bolstered by a dynamic platoon advantage and a premium #3 batting position, positioning him to drive in the bulk of our runs.\n\nThe decision to bench **Mickey Moniak** was the most difficult of the morning, as his 39.40 score landed agonizingly close to our 40.00 floor. While he shows flashes of potential, the combination of a tough 3.34 xERA matchup against Montgomery and a poor platoon outlook neutralized his upside, forcing him to the pine to preserve our limited game caps. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Seiya Suzuki** and **Trevor Story**; both are battling the headwinds of sub-3.30 xERA opposing starters, with **Trevor Story** specifically hampered by an elite-level arm in Luzardo. Though **James Wood** faces a stingy 3.01 xERA starter in Burns, his elite #1 batting position and a 5% wind-out factor keep him as a viable, albeit high-risk, option for stolen base production. As we monitor the wire, we remain ready to pivot if the weather reports or late-scratch risks manifest, particularly with **Corbin Carroll** currently sidelined on an off-day, depriving us of our primary speed weapon.",
